    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0549" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1949v04/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.014/3–1749: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Certain Diplomatic and Consular Offices
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d304-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-17T02:00:00-05:00">March 17, 1949—2
                            a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Reference] Depcirtel Nov. 26, 1948, 3 a.
                        m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d304-f2"/> In replying to official inquiries re
                        Itcols you may state present US position: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Somaliland be placed under UN trusteeship system with Italy as admin
                            auth under Trusteeship Agreement to he negotiated between Ital and
                                TC.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Eritrea—Cession to Ethio all of Eritrea except Western Province, Itals
                            formerly resident in Eritrea allowed to return to their homes.
                            Appropriate guaranties sought to protect human rights all inhabitants
                            territory, thus providing protection rights both Itals resident Eritrea
                            and those who may return.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>US remains committed support UK trusteeship for Cyrenaica.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>US favors minimum period of trusteeship in order achieve independence
                            for inhabitants of Libya at earliest practicable date.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>Disposition Western Province of Eritrea, Tripolitania and Fezzan being
                            given further consideration. Will inform soonest.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d304-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d304-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to American diplomatic missions at Ankara, Athens, Baghdad, Bangkok, Cairo,
                    Canberra, Jidda, Kabul, Karachi, Manila, Nanking (repeated to Canton), New
                    Delhi, Pretoria, Rangoon, Tehran, Wellington, Addis Ababa, Beirut, Damascus, and
                    Monrovia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d304-f2" n="2" xml:id="d304-f2-content">
                <p>For text, see <ref target="frus1948v03#pg_961">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1948, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, p. 961</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
